A //plumb: directive on an all-blank variable spec declares nothing to wire and
is rejected, rather than silently doing nothing. (A single blank var is the
conversion form, var _ T = expr, handled separately.)
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
error-is: ErrBlankProvider
-- example.com/app/a.go --
package app

//plumb:build
var _, _ = 1, 2
